<title>SWITZERLAND: Barry Callebaut says British MMC approves merger.</title>
<headline>Barry Callebaut says British MMC approves merger.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-06-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chocolate maker and cocoa bean processor Barry Callebaut AG said Britain's Monopolies and Mergers Commission had approved the merger between Barry and Callebaut. &quot;The United States, Germany, Italy and France had already approved of the merger,&quot; it said in a statement. &quot;Only Belgian authorities have refused so far to grant their approval.&quot;</p>
<p>Chief executive Pierre Vermaut said he could not understand Belgium's reluctance and said he still hoped to win approval there eventually.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
